{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope.eq_const_mul_of_hratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope.eq_const_mul_of_hratio","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RigidityReductionScope.lean#L76-L83","doc":"The pointwise corollary, in the form the application consumes: off the\ndivisor, `hratio` already delivers `Ψ = c·Φ`. Stated to make the circularity\nconcrete — this is `uniqueUpToScalar`'s own conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope.hratio_iff_conclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RigidityReductionScope.hratio_iff_conclusion","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RigidityReductionScope.lean#L61-L74","doc":"**The reduction is an identity, not a reduction.** Given double periodicity\nof the ratio, \"the ratio is entire\" and \"the ratio is constant\" are the same\nstatement. Forward is the Liouville step; backward is that constants are\ndifferentiable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}